  "implementation": {
    "network": "Input queue wakes socket select with a bounded nonblocking pipe. Active loopback snapshots target 30 Hz, remote snapshots keep the 95 ms gate. Terrain and output-queue limits stay unchanged.",
    "history": "Wire motion rows are incremental with one overlap; the connection rebuilds up to 18 ticks before coalescing. Full sync/reconnect snapshots carry complete history. Shot tracks retain birth/end samples.",
    "delay": "Starts at 4.5 ticks. After 12 arrivals, target is max(interval p95, interval median + jitter p95) * 30 + 0.5 ticks, clamped to 1.5\u20134.5. Uses 60 socket-arrival samples; shrink limited to two ticks/second; growth immediate. Stable synthetic 30 Hz reaches 1.5 ticks, 10 Hz reaches 3.5; 130 ms bursts raise it to 4.4. Legacy snapshots retain 4.5.",
    "audio": "Local input plays after successful enqueue through the existing pending-action gate. Match/player/sequence receipts suppress every matching authoritative report, including fire/build pairs. Cache bounded to 96 receipts. Optional room checkpoint metadata preserves receipts across restart without changing simulation state.",
    "voices": "Twelve preloaded effect sources plus separate looping music. Reuse stopped sources first and call alSourceStop before rebinding. Protect local reports from ambient voice stealing. Local cues and authoritative attack reports bypass the 65 ms ambient throttle; no audio playback queue or gameplay file reads.",
    "root_causes": [
      "Input enqueue did not wake the 40 ms connection select.",
      "Local snapshots used the same ~100 ms cadence as remote peers.",
      "Fixed 150 ms playback buffering delayed all local reports.",
      "Global cue throttling could discard valid attack sounds during catch-up."
    ]
  },
